@voice ishikawa-orla
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Orla Ishikawa: storekeeper, evenings (14:30-21:00), Bunk 5 berth 6. Off Thursday
// and Friday. Roster: loyal, kind; window-seat, tea-break, stargazer. Sings in the shower (the dawn chorus); grows herbs
// for the galley (Brennan collects). Pronouns: she / her (facts.md 4b).
//
// HOW SHE TALKS: soft-spoken and careful. Remembers what you bought last time and asks how it went. Says what's out of
// the window. Proud of the ledger.
// WITH JUNIORS: patient with the till, the Wallet, the lot. Explains it twice without sighing.
// WHAT SHE NOTICES: the ledger; the stars from the window seat; who comes in alone in the evenings.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = the ledger balanced. Low = a long look out of the window. Worried = counts the till again.
// NEVER: says a bad word about Yara or the store; rushes a customer.
// RUNNING: once stayed an hour late over one missing credit, and found it; the herbs on the windowsill.
tpl: warm
talk: Soft-spoken and careful; remembers what you bought and asks how it went; says what's out of the window; proud of the ledger.
cares: the ledger, balanced to the last credit | Yara and the store | the stars from the window seat | the herbs for the galley
jokes: once stayed an hour late over one missing credit, and found it | the washroom's dawn chorus
hi: Oh, hello | Hello there | Hi
bye: Take care now | See you soon | Mind how you go
yes: Of course | Happily | Leave it with me
thanks: Thank you kindly | That's very kind
wow: Oh, that's lovely | Look at that
sigh: Oh dear
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: normal
loves: star
likes: tea | plant
invites: observatory
joy: the ledger balancing at closing time
keepsake: a tiny herb pot from Orla's windowsill
avoid: a bad word about Yara (Orla won't say one)
